PINBLINK - drive a 40-pin header pin from native code.

Language features
  - SEED_EXPORT; the seed GPIO API (pin mode, digital write, timing)
  - reaching the Pi 4's header through the services table

Try it
  SEED h%, "PINBLINK.SED"
    n% = CALL(h%, 17, 10)        REM pin 17, 10 blinks

Build it on the machine
  grow pinblink          # -> build/PINBLINK.SED
It is also prebuilt in /SEED as PINBLINK.SED, ready to use.

